  <section class="section legal-page" id="main-content" style="padding-top:120px;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:800px;">
      <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: May 14, 2026</p>

      <h2>Our Commitment to Accessibility</h2>
      <p>CC3PO LLC is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. We continually improve the user experience for everyone and apply the relevant accessibility standards.</p>
      <p>This website is designed to conform to <strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> (with ongoing improvements toward WCAG 2.2 AA), in alignment with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Section 508 of the Rehabilitation Act, and California Government Code § 11135.</p>
      <p><strong>We sell compliance services — and we hold ourselves to the same standard.</strong> Accessibility isn't just a service we offer; it's a principle we live by.</p>

      <h2>What We're Doing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Regular Audits:</strong> We conduct periodic accessibility audits using both automated tools and manual testing with assistive technologies</li>
        <li><strong>Keyboard Navigation:</strong> All interactive elements are reachable and operable via keyboard alone, with visible focus indicators</li>
        <li><strong>Screen Reader Support:</strong> Semantic HTML structure, ARIA labels, and proper heading hierarchy ensure compatibility with leading screen readers (JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver)</li>
        <li><strong>Color Contrast:</strong> All text meets WCAG AA minimum contrast ratios (4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text)</li>
        <li><strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Content reflows properly at 320px width and 200% zoom without loss of functionality</li>
        <li><strong>Form Accessibility:</strong> All forms include proper labels, error messaging, and are navigable by assistive technology</li>
        <li><strong>Motion & Animation:</strong> No content relies solely on animation or motion; respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Standards &amp; Conformance</h2>
      <p>We align our digital properties with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> — Web Content Accessibility Guidelines</li>
        <li><strong>Section 508</strong> — Rehabilitation Act of 1973, as amended</li>
        <li><strong>ADA Title II &amp; III</strong> — Americans with Disabilities Act</li>
        <li><strong>CA Government Code § 11135</strong> — State accessibility requirements</li>
        <li><strong>AB 434</strong> — California state agency homepage certification support</li>
        <li><strong>EN 301 549</strong> — European accessibility requirements for ICT products and services</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
      <p>Despite our best efforts, some accessibility limitations may exist:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Content:</strong> Embedded content from third-party services (analytics, form providers, chat widgets) may have accessibility characteristics outside our direct control. We actively evaluate these services and advocate for accessibility improvements.</li>
        <li><strong>Legacy Documents:</strong> Some archived PDFs or documents may not be fully accessible. Contact us for accessible alternatives.</li>
        <li><strong>Continuous Improvement:</strong> Accessibility is an ongoing effort. We prioritize fixes based on user impact and regulatory requirements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Accessibility Services</h2>
      <p>We provide accessibility audit and remediation services to help organizations meet their compliance obligations:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>WCAG 2.1/2.2 AA auditing (automated + manual testing)</li>
        <li>Section 508 compliance assessment</li>
        <li>AB 434 certification support for California agencies</li>
        <li>VPAT / Accessibility Conformance Report (ACR) preparation</li>
        <li>Remediation guidance and implementation</li>
        <li>Ongoing monitoring and re-testing</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/accessibility" style="color:var(--accent);">Learn about our accessibility services →</a></p>

      <h2>Feedback &amp; Contact</h2>
      <p>We welcome your feedback on the accessibility of this website. If you encounter accessibility barriers, please contact us:</p>
      <div style="background:var(--bg-card);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:24px;margin-top:16px;">
        <p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>CC3PO LLC</strong></p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:8px;">16299 Adobe Way, Lathrop, CA 95330</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:8px;">📧 <a href="mailto:accessibility@cc3po.com">accessibility@cc3po.com</a></p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:8px;">📞 <a href="tel:+12094236633">209-423-6633</a></p>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:16px;">We aim to respond to accessibility feedback within <strong>2 business days</strong> and to propose a solution within <strong>10 business days</strong>.</p>

      <h2>Formal Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you wish to file a formal complaint regarding accessibility, you may contact:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>U.S. Department of Justice:</strong> <a href="https://www.ada.gov/file-a-complaint/" style="color:var(--accent);">ADA complaint process</a></li>
        <li><strong>California Department of Rehabilitation:</strong> For state-related accessibility complaints</li>
      </ul>

      <div style="margin-top:48px;text-align:center;">
        <a href="/" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Home</a>
      </div>
